"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K4XA2FF31S0T7V9\",\"title\":\"EcoFix Kenya — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"EcoFix Kenya\",\"Terraton\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"62NK\",\"Crediting period\",\"01 Jan 2026 to 01 Jan 2031\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"62NK\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.2\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"14 Jul 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"15 May 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://terraton.ai\",\"t\":\"Terraton\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.2\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.2\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JRST6G781S06QD2\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JRST6G781S06QD2/prj_1K4XA2FF31S0T7V9/pjd_1KXFRTEZM1S03Y8X/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JRST6G781S06QD2/prj_1K4XA2FF31S0T7V9/pjd_1KRNXSSXB1S0N4K7/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nEcoFix Kenya\\nTerraton\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\n62NK\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jan 2026 to 01 Jan 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.2\\nSummary\\n\\nEcoFix Kenya converts croton nut husk residues collected by smallholder farmers and local aggregators into climate solutions. Our Nanyuki facility converts croton nut husks into biochar, locking away carbon while restoring soils. With sustainable feedstock partnerships, advanced pyrolysis technology, and farmer-centered compost use, we deliver high-impact carbon removals and resilient agriculture.\\n\\nKenya\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 13 Jun 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n14 Jul 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n15 May 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"